Z||000000||loafer87gt||11-02-2001||12:48 AM||||This site is kinda creepy. I just plugged in my info and it told me I was going to die on Christmas of 2050. Yeesh, I kinda wanted to live longer than 73  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR> <A HREF="http://www.deathclock.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.deathclock.com/</A> ||||reg||11
Z||000001||frontal lobe||11-02-2001||01:16 AM||||They seem to be just basing it on an average life expectancy of a NEWBORN male being 74.  <P>Kind of creepy fun, but not very accurate.<P>Plus, you aren't a newborn.  Example:  average life expectancy of a 50 year old is 86 years old.  The longer you live, the longer your life expectancy.<P>So let's hear it--how long DID you want to live?||||reg||1
Z||000002||loafer87gt||11-02-2001||01:24 AM||||I hope to live to be at least a hundred. My family genealogy must have some weird genes as I have several relatives who have lived past the age of a 100. In fact, my great aunt is now 106 years old, and she was just moved into a seniors home two years ago. My grandpa, who died five years ago after breaking his hip and suffering from a stroke, farmed his own land till his death at the age of 86. My dad is now 63, and I swear he looks like he is in his early forties. I always get ticked off how I get ID' everywhere I go for looking so young, but I'll proably be laughin down the road. <P>So whos going to be the longest living forum member?||||reg||10
